body:
We're sorry!

We do have an internal channel to report problems, esp. that many of them end up being configuration-driven. While we cannot funnel people to *always* use it before writing on the bug tracker here, we will make a better job of advertising the internal channels from now on.

@gvanrossum, would it be helpful to reword `CONTRIBUTING.md` to explicitly address first-time bug reporters? For example, @carljm pointed out that it's important for us to always ask for a minimal repro using a clean virtualenv with mypy master installed in it. That would help in situations like this issue where integration is hiding what is happening under the hood.
